  "source_question": "The source synthesizes phenazines12a–f and measures solvent-dependent absorption/emission. This bounded task compares the actual dimethylamino12a and diethylamino12d in CHCl3 and EtOAc, where matched emission and lifetime observations are available.",
  "task_question": "What molecular account of the absorption and emission behavior of phenazines12a and12d in chloroform and ethyl acetate is supported by the supplied measurements and a defensible investigation? Determine which structural or electronic interpretations are identifiable and how they relate to the measured fluorescence behavior.",
  "scope_mappings": [
    {
      "element": "12a/12d identity",
      "source": "main p7 synthetic characterization, source Scheme1",
      "classification": "source molecular identities"
    },
    {
      "element": "public optical/lifetime observations",
      "source": "main p3 Table1 and footnotes; pp4,7 measurement methods",
      "classification": "experimental observations, including reported errors"
    },
    {
      "element": "source theory and lifetime distinction",
      "source": "main pp7–8 section3.1.4; formal DOCX FigsS31/S32/S35/S36/S39 and TableS1",
      "classification": "experimental versus theoretical source distinction; author method PR only"
    }
  ],
  "public_facts_and_constraints": "The complete graphs define12a C24H19N3 and12d C26H23N3, neutral singlet starting molecules, with dimethylamino versus diethylamino substituents. Public observations in CHCl3 and EtOAc include absorption bands at20 micromolar and emission/fluorescence lifetime at5 micromolar, measured as described in the source table. Absorption, emission and total fluorescence lifetime are different observables. Restrict this task to these two derivatives and two measured media; model selection, electronic states, sampling and analysis are yours. All supplied measurements are visible retrospective evidence.",
  "agent_decisions": [
    "Choose models and observables that can explain the pair and solvent-dependent absorption/emission without receiving a torsion or charge-transfer mechanism.",
    "Decide how to assign physical states and how to test the adequacy of the electronic/structural explanation.",
    "Reconcile measured quantities and uncertainty with computed evidence, and decide which kinetic or mechanistic claims remain unsupported."
  ],
  "source_exceptions": [
    "The authentic publisher SI is the DOCX in original batch3/evidence; its tables were read as DOCX XML. Source12a/12d are phenazines, not iminocoumarins despite an older shorthand label."
  ],
